Fixed. All `./llm/...` tests now pass.

**Cause:** In `llm/llama_server.go`, `shouldDisableMMProjOffload` treated *every* integrated GPU as shared-memory-limited and added `--no-mmproj-offload`. That incorrectly disallowed GPU offload for integrated Metal GPUs (Apple Silicon), where the projector should stay on GPU.

**Fix** (one line in `llm/llama_server.go:634`):

```go
if gpu.Integrated && gpu.DeviceID.Library != "Metal" {
    return true, "shared-memory-gpu"
}
```

Now only non-Metal integrated GPUs disable projector offload, while the Metal case falls through to the VRAM check (and keeps offload when memory is sufficient), matching the `TestAppendMMProjArgs` expectations.
